<p>Israel and Lebanon agreed to extend a U.S.-mediated ceasefire by 45 days after two days of talks in Washington, the U.S. State Department said Friday. The April 16 cessation of hostilities, announced by President Trump and due to expire Sunday, will remain in effect as negotiations continue, State Department spokesman Tommy Pigott said. The State Department said political negotiations aimed at a permanent agreement are scheduled for June 2-3, and the Pentagon will convene military delegations on May 29 for a security track. Violence continued during the talks: Israeli strikes wounded dozens in Lebanon as the talks entered their second day, The Hindu reported, and Al Jazeera said Israeli attacks killed seven in Lebanon the same day. Israel has said some strikes are not covered by the truce; Lebanon has demanded an end to Israeli attacks and Israel&#x27;s occupation of Lebanese territory.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CIfc4chJHcX4ihRNJqfTcctPdwvXS1_tMLLZSzLovoJWKeD6jxWTbLCALjhFSC7Hi-PrUGLXd7_f4yMns2YDNqZzR4Rs06eED_VEHMoQoGIXWjthm06IauQBqX8mssiaDZdJebQW9_nLfxdohH-2cNg5E5uaKClGfJ7J5X2B74GMoIaUKIp_ybXtcfSB2oIUSfJdzwWI73axgAGK99NOuwutsOKCdlv17r9D0jWdVLtyWGpeZ4lICLfQpL3jBQitXgbqMdVD9LcF3-G2FA' alt='The U.S. hosted two days of talks between Israel and Lebanon.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Hezbollah role: Hezbollah was not part of the Washington diplomacy and has opposed direct Lebanese talks with Israel. Israel accuses the group of firing into northern Israel.</li><li>Border fighting: DW said the truce reduced the volume of fighting, but violations remained frequent, particularly in southern Lebanon.</li></ul><blockquote>We hope these discussions will advance lasting peace between the two countries, full recognition of each other&#x27;s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and establishing genuine security along their shared border - Tommy Pigott</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. State Department: Pigott described the Washington meetings a